Z||000000||DaveL||10-06-2000||03:34 PM||||I've just got to figure this out. Every time my girlfriend and I go driving around in my SE, there seems to be a very odd sort of noise from the general direction of the passenger seat. It gets noticeably worse if I really tweak it around a corner, or floor it up to redline. Its an extremely irritating type of sound, a lot like scraping your fingernails on a chalkboard. Kind of a cross between a buzzard screaching, and your mom yelling at you. The kicker is it never happens when I'm driving alone!<BR>Any thoughts?||||reg||12
Z||000001||deceler8||10-06-2000||03:39 PM||||Just how heavy is your girlfriend ?<P>Just kidding.<P>Your description sounds like a mount (or dogbone) is either loose or worn out. If your bone isn't properly tightened, the engine end can slip in the mounting bracket.<P>Only other thing that comes to mind is that you're loading up the right rear wheel bearing with a passenger and a fast takeoff and the bearing is going bad.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||10-06-2000||04:06 PM||||Could it be the seat is coming loose from the floor mounts.||||reg||3
Z||000003||sdm1964||10-06-2000||04:51 PM||||Sure it's not your girlfriend screaming in delight, because she is being driven around in one totally awsome ride? Or your driving scares her to death? Your choice....||||reg||14
Z||000004||2xsess||10-06-2000||06:37 PM||||I'd check the seat mount bolts first. Have your gf listen and see if it is coming from the front or rear of the car.<P>Does it do it when you drive around with anyone else in the car? Maybe your car is posessed and doesn't like women.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
