Z||000013||DavidHenshaw||10-07-2000||08:12 PM||||Dave, I know exactly what the noise is. It has absolutely nothing to do with your car other than the fact that your car has a passenger seat. As you round a corner right or left at any speed faster than walk your passenger's shirt, jacket, or whatever is rubbing aginst the leather strip about 3/4 of the way up on the passenger's seat. Believe it!<P>I had the same thing when my wife is with me. I was saying, "What is that noise, what is that noise." It sounds like something in the engine. My wife said, "Its my jacket rubbing aginst the seat." And sure enough she could reproduce the exact sound by moving from side to side while we were parked.<P>Dave<P>86 GT fastback||||reg||1
Z||000014||DaveL||10-07-2000||08:42 PM||||She was obviously wearing corduroy...<BR>Funny, I'm not sure how you knew, but there was a sharp pounding pain in one shoulder, a jabbing pain in the ribs, a nasty ringing in my right ear, and extreme pressure on my right knee that almost cut off all circulation. Maybe it is the fan pipe outlet?No, just need a replacement girlfriend. I don't think a discount imported part will do. Have to go back to the factory.<BR>Thanks for the laughs! ||||reg||10
